cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use statdrift, please cite it as below."
title: statdrift
abstract: >-
  A frozen battery of statistical calls run under every minor SciPy release from 1.9 to
  1.18 and every statsmodels release from 0.13.5 to 0.15.0, in pinned environments that
  share a toolchain across each diffed pair. It measures how often outputs change, how often
  a p-value crosses 0.05 or 0.01, and how often the release notes named the function.
type: software
authors:
  - name: h-a-forster
repository-code: "https://github.com/h-a-forster/statdrift"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-06"
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - statistical software
  - scipy
  - statsmodels
  - software drift
